{"name":"Aztec Brick","hex":"#9e8352","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardened rectangular block of mud, clay etc., used for building.","Such hardened mud, clay, etc. considered collectively, as a building material."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build, line, or form with bricks.","To make into bricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aztecs","blocks":[{"text":"The Aztecs were a Mesoamerican civilization that flourished in central Mexico from about 1300 to 1521. The Aztec people included different ethnic groups of central Mexico, particularly those who spoke Nahuatl. Aztec culture was organized into city-states (altepetl), some of which joined to form alliances, political confederations, or empires. The Aztec Empire was a confederation of three city-states established in 1427: Tenochtitlan, Tetzcoco, and Tlacopan. Although the term Aztecs is often narrowly restricted to the Mexica of Tenochtitlan, it is also broadly used to refer to Nahua polities or peoples of central Mexico in the pre-Hispanic era, as well as the Spanish colonial era (1521–1821)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Aztec_Empire.png/330px-Aztec_Empire.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aztecs","wikidata":"Q12542"},{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick"